By sharding the checkpoint file, the communication overhead is reduced because each node only needs to communicate with a subset of the other nodes to access the necessary model parameters. Additionally, checkpoint sharding allows for greater scalability because each node can process a portion of the model in parallel, reducing the amount of time required to complete each training iteration.

