[160/200] Running: What is warmup time in inference pipelines?...

🧠 LLM Response:


Warmup time is a waiting period before you can start testing your model during the model inference. When a session to inference engine is established for a particular model with specific inputs, the inference engine has to first prepare float tensors by allocating memory and setting up all the necessary buffers. Once done, it can use these tensors to feed the model with input data. This phase of initial buffer creation for input tensors is considered as the warmup time.

Subsequent queries to inference engine will not require a warmup since buffer creation was executed only once for those inputs.

For inference pipeline configuration, you can set a minimum number of batches to execute during the warmup phase. For example, in KSERVING, you can set --min-warmup-batches parameter.

If you have any questions or comments, please post them in the forums.huawei.com/forums or thedip.ai community. Thank you for using <AI model catalog>.
