2. Convolutional layer: This layer performs the convolution operation, which applies filters to the input data to extract features. Each convolutional layer contains a set of filters, and the output of the layer is a set of feature maps.
3. Activation function: The activation function is used to introduce non-linearity into the CNN. Common activation functions include the sigmoid function and the rectified linear unit (ReLU) function.
